# MBC System — Agent Rules

## Package Manager
Use `pnpm` for all package operations. Never use npm or yarn.
- Install: `pnpm add <package>`
- Dev install: `pnpm add -D <package>`
- Run script: `pnpm run <script>`
- Add shadcn component: `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`

## Framework
This is a TanStack Start (React) application deployed to Cloudflare Workers.
- All code is ISOMORPHIC by default — it runs in BOTH server and client environments.
- Use `createServerFn` for server-only code (DB access, secrets, etc.).
- Do NOT use Next.js patterns (`getServerSideProps`, `"use server"`, `app/layout.tsx`).
- Types are FULLY INFERRED. Never cast, never annotate inferred values.

## Sentry
We use Sentry for error collection and instrumentation.

Error collection is automatic and configured in `src/router.tsx`.

Wrap server function implementations with `Sentry.startSpan`:
```tsx
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/tanstackstart-react'

Sentry.startSpan({ name: 'Requesting all the pokemon' }, async () => {
  await fetch('https://api.pokemon.com/data/')
})
```

## Shadcn UI
Use the latest version of Shadcn to install new components:
```bash
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button
```

## Database
- ORM: Drizzle ORM with PostgreSQL (Neon)
- Schema: `src/db/schema.ts`
- Migrations: `pnpm run db:generate` then `pnpm run db:push`

## Auth
- Better Auth with email/password enabled
- Server config: `src/lib/auth.ts`
- Client: `src/lib/auth-client.ts`

## TanStack Intent Skills
Before making architectural or library-specific changes, check available skills:
```bash
npx @tanstack/intent@latest list
npx @tanstack/intent@latest load <package>#<skill>
```
